## 3. `@getmaapp/signal-wasm@0.6.6` — the E2EE engine

- Declared license: **AGPL-3.0-only** (`license` field of the package
  `package.json`, confirmed via the registry on 2026-09-09).
- The package's own `LICENSE` file is **1,174 bytes / 29 lines — a notice, not
  the license text**. It states `Copyright (C) 2026 The Cannabis App`, that
  the WASM bridge is built on libsignal (AGPL-3.0), and it grants "either
  version 3 of the License, or (at your option) any later version".
- **Recorded ambiguity, not resolved here:** that notice says "or any later
  version" while the same package declares `AGPL-3.0-only` in its metadata.
  enough. adopts the narrower **AGPL-3.0-only** and does not rely on the
  "or later" option. If the upstream text is authoritative for the "or later"
  grant, taking the narrower option remains permitted; the discrepancy is
  flagged so it is not mistaken for an oversight.
- What is actually conveyed to the browser, byte-for-byte:
  `signal_wasm_bg.wasm` (797,749 bytes, SHA-256
  `71b456b8a1bfc93111be86fdff9726ed397de55f223ee9136dab619a6620d6c1`) and
  `signal_wasm.js` (78,213 bytes, SHA-256
  `c72af7ae13a17fca0b0c2a2b8acb948c9eb9c71a17f9c4194c53bdf2ab883410`).
  These hashes are the audited values in `docs/e2ee-2c-provenance.md` §1 and
  are asserted on every CI run by `npm run verify:signal-wasm`
  (`docs/e2ee-f5-supply-chain.md`).
- **Attribution does not survive the build:** neither the shipped WASM nor the
  JS glue carries any license or copyright text (verified 2026-09-09: zero
  case-insensitive matches for "agpl" or "copyright" in `signal_wasm.js` and
  `signal_wasm.d.ts`). A user who only downloads the bundle therefore receives
  no attribution from it, which is why `LICENSE` is additionally served as a
  same-origin static file at the deployed site root (§5).
- No forking or source modification of the package is made; it is consumed
  unmodified from the npm registry. The build was **not** reproduced
  (`docs/e2ee-2c-provenance.md`, `docs/e2ee-f5-supply-chain.md` §5), so the
  correspondence between those bytes and the upstream source commit is
  asserted by hash pin, not by a reproducible build.

