## 5. Distribution, conveyed object code, and source availability

- The public instance is a static site; the built JavaScript and the 797 kB
  WASM asset are transferred to, and executed by, every visitor. That is
  conveyance of object code, and visitors also interact with the service over
  a network, so the source-availability obligations of AGPL-3.0 §§ 13 and 5(c)
  apply to the released version.
- Complete Corresponding Source for any released version is the public
  repository <https://github.com/hpmine42/enough> at the corresponding tag or
  commit (releases are published there with matching tags): the application
  source, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, the build configuration
  (`vite.config.ts`, `scripts/`), the SQL migrations, and CI definitions —
  i.e. everything needed to regenerate the conveyed app. The `LICENSE` text
  itself is additionally served at the site root as a same-origin static file
  (`public/LICENSE` → `/LICENSE`), because the bundle carries none (§3).
- Self-hosting is permitted under the same terms, and the same obligations
  transfer to the self-hoster (`docs/self-hosting.md`).

